This is fixed in [v1](https://github.com/openai/openai-python/discussions/631) which was just released!

You can specify a custom base URL by passing the `base_url` argument to the constructor, e.g. `OpenAI(base_url='...')`.

If you need to use custom paths then you can write your own [event hook](https://www.python-httpx.org/advanced/#event-hooks) to do so, for example:
```py
import httpx
from openai import OpenAI

def update_base_url(request: httpx.Request) -> None:
    # rewrite the path segment to what the proxy expects
    if request.url.path == "/v1/chat/completions":
